# Whether every release must carry the ML-DSA-65 signature beside the Ed25519 one.
#
# The release workflow reads this file. While it holds only comments, as now, it
# requires nothing: the second signature is required only while
# keyring/glyndor-release-mldsa65.b64 holds a key or its secret is set. Once a line
# reading exactly
#
#   required
#
# is added (without the indent above), every release must carry it: a release
# whose anchor holds no key, whose signing secret is not set, or whose second
# signature is missing or does not verify is refused. Taking the line out again is
# what retires the second signature, a change of its own in a reviewed pull request.
#
# Printable ASCII and line feeds only. Any line that is not a comment, blank or
# exactly "required" stops the release instead of being read as "not required".
